  { id: 'volume', label: 'Why cheap rates wear cars out' },
  { id: 'owner-operated', label: 'Owner-operated, not investor-operated' },
  { id: 'check', label: 'What to check before you book' },
  { id: 'faq', label: 'Common questions' },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How do you stop rental cars smelling of smoke?',
    a: `By detailing every car between rentals rather than between bookings that happen to look dirty, then running an ozone treatment through the cabin once the detail is finished. Ozone oxidises what is left in the headliner and the vents, which is the part no wipe-down reaches. It only works on a cabin that has already been cleaned properly — run it over a dirty car and it masks the smell rather than removing it, which is why the order matters.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What does well kept actually mean for an exotic rental in Miami?',
    a: `Three things you can check rather than take on trust: the car is detailed between every rental, the photographs on the listing are of that exact car, and the person handing you the keys can answer questions about it. Anything else is a claim.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Why are some Miami exotic rentals so much cheaper?',
    a: `Usually volume. A lower rate needs more rental days to make the same return, and more days in a year is more wear, more handovers and less time for the car to be put right between them. The discount is real — it is funded by the condition of the car.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What is owner-operated and why does it matter?',
    a: `It means the person who sets the price is the person who hands over the keys and pays for the detailing. There is no desk between the decision and the consequence. Every price, deposit and fee quoted on this site is one Robert sets and honors himself.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I get the exact car in the photographs?',
    a: `Yes. Every listing shows the actual car, not a stock image of the model. If you booked the purple Huracán EVO, that is what arrives — which is also why the condition in those photographs is something we have to keep true.`,
